// Deadlock-watchdog runtime hooks (bindings to compiler-emitted C).
// 
// The compiler always emits these three symbols in the C prelude: real
// implementations when the program uses `fork` (they feed the M:N scheduler's
// blocked-task counter so the watchdog thread can detect a global stall), and
// no-op stubs otherwise. They are only exercised when FUN_DEADLOCK_WATCHDOG_MS
// arms the watchdog; with it unset, the channel layer never calls them.

// Mark the current thread as entering a blocking channel wait.
pub fun __fun_wd_enter_wait();

// Mark the current thread as leaving a blocking channel wait (records progress).
pub fun __fun_wd_leave_wait();

// Print a "possible deadlock" diagnostic to stderr.
// 
// Params:
// - blocked_or_count: blocked task count (scheduler) or channel occupancy
// - pending_or_cap: pending tasks (scheduler) or channel capacity
// - stall_ms: how long no progress has been observed
pub fun __fun_wd_warn(num blocked_or_count, num pending_or_cap, num stall_ms);
